What is the output of the following Java program combining a custom checked exception with cause wrapping?
```java
import java.io.IOException;
class StorageException extends Exception {
    private final String resourceId;
    public StorageException(String message, String resId, Throwable cause) {
        super(message, cause);
        this.resourceId = resId;
    }
    public String getResourceId() { return resourceId; }
}
public class StorageDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            try {
                throw new IOException("Read error");
            } catch (IOException ioe) {
                throw new StorageException("Failed", "vol-101", ioe);
            }
        } catch (StorageException se) {
            System.out.print(se.getResourceId() + "-" + se.getCause().getMessage());
        }
    }
}
```

