What is the output of the following Java program demonstrating polymorphism with custom exception hierarchies?
```java
class ServiceFaultException extends RuntimeException {
    public String getSeverity() { return "LOW"; }
}
class CriticalFaultException extends ServiceFaultException {
    @Override
    public String getSeverity() { return "CRITICAL"; }
}
public class FaultDispatcher {
    public static void report(ServiceFaultException fault) {
        System.out.print(fault.getSeverity());
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            throw new CriticalFaultException();
        } catch (ServiceFaultException ex) {
            report(ex);
        }
    }
}
```
